{"term":"evolve","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:07cae19077cf24333d","definition":"To move (something) in regular procession through a system.","example":"The animal soul sooner expands and evolves it self to its full orb and extent than the humane Soul","pos":"verb","synonyms":["develop","progress"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["coevolve","co-evolve","evolvability","evolvingly","microevolve","nonevolving","photoevolve","reevolve"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evolve#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e51fafb88c2accf87c","definition":"To change or transform (something).","example":"Over several years the author evolved the story originally drafted as a novella into a real epic.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["develop","convert","develop","draw","evolve","metamorphize","metamorphose","reconvert","shift","transfigurate","transfigure","transform","transmogrify","transmute","transume"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["coevolve","co-evolve","evolvability","evolvingly","microevolve","nonevolving","photoevolve","reevolve"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evolve#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:caac03c2da606bc676","definition":"To cause (something) to come into being or develop.","example":"You will remove the pig, place it in the car, and drive it to my house in Wiltshire. That is the plan I have evolved.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["contrive","generate","bring forth","cause","contrive","create","ferment","forge","develop","engender","evolve","generate","gin up","innate","form","forthbring","make","produce","spawn"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["coevolve","co-evolve","evolvability","evolvingly","mic