iki/evolve#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:76d8698e95d5dc36cb","definition":"To wind or unwind (something).","example":"And come, my Muſe! that lov'ſt the ſylvan ſhade, / Evolve the mazes, and the miſt diſpel; / Tranſlate the ſong; convince my doubting maid / No ſolemn Derviſe can explain ſo vvell— […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["coevolve","co-evolve","evolvability","evolvingly","microevolve","nonevolving","photoevolve","reevolve"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evolve#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:acdc4097c9d6865ab9","definition":"To move in regular procession through a system.","example":"[T]he principles which Art involves, Science alone evolves.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["coevolve","co-evolve","evolvability","evolvingly","microevolve","nonevolving","photoevolve","reevolve"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evolve#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2681d646524aefd526","definition":"To change, to transform.","example":"What began as a few lines of code has now evolved into a million-line behemoth.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["coevolve","co-evolve","evolvability","evolvingly","microevolve","nonevolving","photoevolve","reevolve"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evolve#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:38e0e6ecbafba2d1dd","definition":"Of a trait; to develop within a population through biological evolution.","example":"How long ago